re basically Mid City. Whatevs, I sure hope they open up their radius a little bit. They have a window inside Banks St Bar. It's convenient. This little place is awesome."},{"business_id":"p08wWg9hIsvun4l-cfuWRg","review_id":"g1uRPODbLTdDKPPJjf9Hcg","date":"2014-09-18T21:52:08","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9332981109619141,"text_excerpt":"Must be something about this building that puts out good pizzas (get your mind out of the gutter). From when this place was Lazarro's to now, I've always preferred the pies that came from this joint. I also appreciate that you can buy by the slice here as well. They're (slices) large, almost two and a quarter size slices so you've gotta fold em' real New-Yorker style and the thin crust really gives it the authentic, Yankee experience. I went basic and started off trying a slice of cheese and another of pepperoni, both were a pizza - lover's delight. The other selections looked quite appeasing and are definitely on the list of things to try. My only thing is for some odd reason, whenever I..."},{"business_id":"p08wWg9hIsvun4l-cfuWRg","review_id":"W7t_DW6CfpdKQFpdxWBXcA","date":"2014-09-09T21:46:26","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9188479781150818,"text_excerpt":"Just went for first time few days ago. Glad I did. Very good thin crust NY-style pies. Jumps right up the chart to Número Dos of nola pizzerias. Ceaser salad was pretty good too."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
